  "faq": {
    "sectionTitle": "Fragen?",
    "sectionHeading": "Häufig Gestellte Fragen",
    "items": [
      {
        "q": "What is SAMI Summer Course?",
        "a": "SAMI (Sustainable Agrifood Management in Indonesia) is an annual international summer course from Department of Management, IPB University, running since 2017. The 9th edition (2026) is held hybrid 27 July – 15 August, with 14 courses on sustainable agrifood management, essay contest, and field visits in Bogor & Garut."
      },
      {
        "q": "What tracks are available?",
        "a": "Two options: Online Course Track (12 live online sessions, 2 credits) and Online + Site Visit Track (12 online sessions + 2 hybrid courses on campus + field visits, 4 credits)."
      },
      {
        "q": "When is the registration period?",
        "a": "Registration opens 28 April – 17 July 2026, announcement 17 July, and payment deadline 20 July 2026. For fee details, check the program book at https://drive.google.com/file/d/1D1NC92bcacJQB1MCXLwprNpfzdUK8Fk0/view."
      },
      {
        "q": "How to register?",
        "a": "Submit application via ipb.link/submission-sami-2026. Read the full program book at https://drive.google.com/file/d/1D1NC92bcacJQB1MCXLwprNpfzdUK8Fk0/view."
      },
      {
        "q": "When are online courses held?",
        "a": "12 online sessions run 27–31 July 2026 via Zoom. Slides shared via WhatsApp group one day prior, and also on learning portal samiipb.site."
      },
      {
        "q": "What happens during the onsite portion?",
        "a": "Offline participants arrive in Bogor 9 August, attend 2 hybrid courses (10 & 14 August), and 9 field visits in Bogor & Garut from 10–15 August — including IPB Dramaga Campus, Eptilu agrotourism, Mandalagiri coffee cooperative, Margawati sheep/goat center, Bestory dodol production, Sukaregang leather market, Cangkuang Temple, IPB Science Technopark, and Bogor Botanical Garden."
      },
      {
        "q": "Is there a certificate?",
        "a": "Yes. Participants who complete the program receive Certificate of Completion, Certificate of Participation for Essay Contest, and credit transcripts (4 credits for full program, 2 credits for online only) issued by Department of Management IPB University."
      },
      {
        "q": "Is the essay contest mandatory?",
        "a": "The essay contest is part of the project assignment. Groups submit essays (max. 3,000 words) plus presentation, with final presentation 14 August at Start Up Science Technopark, Bogor. Top 3 essays get certificates & cash prizes (1st: IDR 3,000,000, 2nd: IDR 2,000,000, 3rd: IDR 1,000,000), and all accepted essays published in SAMI Proceeding with ISBN."
      },
      {
        "q": "What is the language of instruction?",
        "a": "All sessions and essays use English."
      }
    ]
  },
